  "title": "Cession of Fiji to Britain",
  "summary": "On 10 October 1874 Ratu Seru Cakobau, who styled himself Tui Viti, and other leading Fijian chiefs signed a Deed of Cession at Levuka handing Fiji to the United Kingdom. Britain accepted after earlier refusals. The deed promised to recognise the chiefs' rights so far as consistent with British sovereignty.",
